factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 5 problems
  The reel_script and slides_spec say the Hindu Makkal Katchi executives were arrested because they tried to go to Thiruparankundram, but the article only says they were arrested while trying to travel there, without naming that as the cause of the arrest; the stated cause is an added inference.
  The slides_spec says the two executives 'இருவரும் உடுமலையிலிருந்து புறப்பட முயன்றனர்' and the reel_script says the arrests were at Udumalai bus stand; the article says the arrests happened at the bus stand, which matches, but the slide wording 'வீட்டுக்காவல்' section lumps the house arrests together with 'இதனால் உடுமலையில் பரபரப்பு நிலவியது' which is a causal link not stated in the article.
  The caption and reel_script state that the leaders were 'கட்சியின் மடத்துக்குளம் தெற்கு ஒன்றியத் தலைவர்' housed under house arrest, but the article names Kalimuthu as the Madathukulam South union president; the caption mentions 'Udumalaipettai' tag, which is an English location name not in the article's Tamil text, though the place is consistent.
  The reel_script says Hindu organisation executives in the Udumalai area were placed under house arrest, but the article says the police placed other Hindu organisation executives under house arrest without specifying the area as Udumalai bus stand; the phrase 'உடுமலை பகுதியின்' is a reasonable reading but adds a locational specificity.
  The slides_spec 'hl2' headline and category 'போலீஸ் நடவடிக்கை' are editorial additions not claims from the article, but the caption's 'பரபரப்பு' framing is also an editorial addition.
